  "Question": "Of the \\(500\\) balls in a large bag, \\(80\\%\\) are red and the rest are blue. How many of the red balls must be removed so that \\(75\\%\\) of the remaining balls are red?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( \\ 25 \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\ 50 \\)",
    "C": "\\( \\ 75 \\)",
    "D": "\\( \\ 100 \\)",
    "E": "\\( \\ 150 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Only red balls are removed, so the number of blue balls stays fixed. Initially, blue balls make up \\(100\\%-80\\%=20\\%\\) of the bag, giving\n\\[\n0.20\\cdot500=100\\text{ blue balls}.\n\\]\nWhen \\(75\\%\\) of the remaining balls are red, the other \\(25\\%\\) are blue. Thus the unchanged \\(100\\) blue balls are \\(25\\%\\) of the remaining total. That total must be\n\\[\n100\\div0.25=400\\text{ balls}.\n\\]\nThe number removed is \\(500-400=\\boxed{100}\\), all red. Indeed, the remaining bag has \\(300\\) red and \\(100\\) blue balls, so its red share is \\(300/400=75\\%\\). The answer is choice D.",
